            {
              "id": "art-body",
              "type": "column",
              "props": {
                "span": 9
              },
              "children": [
                {
                  "id": "lede",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "If you run a trucking business, you already know the importance of staying compliant, safe, and ready for the road. A DOT inspection isn't just a regulatory box to check; it's one of the most effective ways to protect your drivers, your equipment, and your bottom line.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full",
                    "anchor": "post-lede"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-intro-1",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "At Sun State International, we see firsthand how a thorough commercial truck inspection helps prevent unexpected breakdowns, costly fines, and unnecessary downtime. And for a hardworking owner-operator or fleet manager, few things matter more than keeping business moving.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-intro-2",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "As a company built on dependability, Sun State International is committed to helping you stay confident and prepared for every mile ahead. Whether you're managing a growing fleet or operating your own truck, understanding what goes into an inspection, and how to prepare for it, can make DOT compliance a whole lot smoother.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "h-what-is-it",
                  "type": "heading",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "What Is a DOT Inspection and Why Does It Matter?",
                    "headingLevel": 2,
                    "align": "left",
                    "anchor": "what-is-it"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-what-is-it-1",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "A DOT inspection is a federally mandated fleet safety inspection designed to ensure your commercial vehicles meet all DOT compliance and FMCSA safety standards. These annual checks verify that your truck is safe to operate and that critical components, such as brakes, tires, lights, coupling devices, and more, are functioning properly. For fleets trying to stay ahead of unexpected repairs, the annual truck inspection is one of the most powerful preventive tools you have.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "h-checklist",
                  "type": "heading",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "A DOT Inspection Checklist: What Inspectors Look For",
                    "headingLevel": 2,
                    "align": "left",
                    "anchor": "checklist"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-checklist-1",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "While every level of DOT inspection varies, most follow a structured process. A well-organized DOT inspection checklist can help you ensure your truck is ready long before an inspector arrives. Key areas examined include:",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "features-checklist-2",
                  "type": "list",
                  "props": {
                    "headingLevel": 2,
                    "columns": 4,
                    "items": [
                      {
                        "label": "Brakes",
                        "desc": "Brake trouble is one of the most common causes of out-of-service orders. Inspectors look for worn components, damaged hoses, and proper adjustment."
                      },
                      {
                        "label": "Tires & Wheels",
                        "desc": "Uneven tread, worn tires, damaged rims, or improper inflation can immediately trigger a violation."
                      },
                      {
                        "label": "Lighting & Electrical",
                        "desc": "Headlights, brake lights, turn signals, warning lights, and wiring. Electrical issues are easy to overlook, yet extremely common."
                      },
                      {
                        "label": "Steering & Suspension",
                        "desc": "Anything affecting maneuverability or stability will be flagged."
                      },
                      {
                        "label": "Fuel Systems",
                        "desc": "Leaks, unsecured tanks, or improper caps can result in serious fines."
                      },
                      {
                        "label": "Coupling Devices",
                        "desc": "These components must be in top condition to ensure trailer and truck connection integrity."
                      },
                      {
                        "label": "Emergency Equipment",
                        "desc": "Fire extinguishers, reflectors, and required safety gear must be present and functional."
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-checklist-3",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "Staying ahead of these areas not only keeps your truck compliant; it protects your investment.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "fig-1",
                  "type": "image",
                  "props": {
                    "width": "full",
                    "image": {
                      "src": "/img/blog/how-a-routine-dot-inspection-keeps-your-fleet-on-the-road/1.jpg",
                      "width": 1280,
                      "height": 853,
                      "alt": "Sun State International technician working under a truck cab during a service bay inspection"
                    }
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "h-hidden-value",
                  "type": "heading",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "The Hidden Value of Routine Commercial Truck Inspections",
                    "headingLevel": 2,
                    "align": "left",
                    "anchor": "hidden-value"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-hidden-value-1",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "A DOT inspection isn't just an annual requirement; it's a chance to extend the life of your equipment and avoid costly downtime. At Sun State International, many of our service customers tell us the same thing: catching something early is always cheaper than losing days on the road. Routine checks also support:",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "checks-hidden-value-2",
                  "type": "check-list",
                  "props": {
                    "items": [
                      {
                        "text": "Greater safety for drivers"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": "More predictable operating costs"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": "Stronger customer trust"
                      },
                      {
                        "text": "Higher resale value"
                      }
                    ]
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "p-hidden-value-3",
                  "type": "text",
                  "props": {
                    "text": "A safer truck protects the people who work hardest for your company. Unexpected repairs cost more than routine maintenance, both in money and lost miles. And a well-maintained truck holds value significantly better than one with spotty repair records.",
                    "align": "left",
                    "width": "full"
                  }
                },
                {
                  "id": "co-hidden-value-4-row",
                  "type": "row",
                  "props": {
                    "gap": 0
                  },
                  "children": [
                    {
                      "id": "co-hidden-value-4",
                      "type": "column",
                      "props": {
                        "span": 12
                      },
                      "styles": {
                        "base": {
                          "borderWidth": 1,
                          "borderStyle": "solid",
